  "note": "Relay pre-E2EE hello record layouts (v1). Generated by an encoder written independently of the Rust implementation, so this fixture locks the specification rather than the code. The session is the same one relay-webcrypto-v1.json pins, so the two files describe one coherent handshake. Every scalar here is a fixed test value and no production key material appears in this file. Signatures cover both offers, so neither side can sign before seeing the peer's ephemeral key: the device therefore opens with an unsigned Offer (0x00 = the IdentityHello minus its signature), the desktop answers with its signed IdentityHello, and only then does the device sign. The pairing secret is the public all-zero 32-byte test vector; it is intentionally unsuitable for production authentication.",
